//! The catalogue of declarative scanners.
//!
//! Every entry here becomes a scanner. Adding support for a new tool is a new
//! `PathRule` and nothing else.
//!
//! Two conventions keep this table honest:
//!
//! * `explanation` is written for someone who has never heard of the tool. It
//!   must say what the data is *and* what happens after it is deleted. "Build
//!   artifacts generated by Xcode" is only half an explanation; "…they are
//!   rebuilt the next time you build, which takes longer once" is the rest.
//! * `risk` is [`RiskLevel::Safe`] only when the owning application regenerates
//!   the data by itself. Anything the user would have to re-download, redo, or
//!   might actually want is [`RiskLevel::Review`].

use spacekeeper_core::{Category, Family, RiskLevel};

use crate::rules::PathRule;

const ALL: &[&str] = &["macos", "linux", "windows"];
const MAC: &[&str] = &["macos"];
const UNIX: &[&str] = &["macos", "linux"];
const LINUX: &[&str] = &["linux"];

/// Every declarative rule SpaceKeeper ships with.
